      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Stop romanticizing this feeling; your description of a dead part of yourself dying suggests a deep depressive episode, not just \"poetic emptiness,\" which is a much more serious and distressing reality than empty metaphors. When you describe feeling like a ghost that has lost its purpose, your brain is likely rewiring to filter out joy and amplify hopelessness, making it physically exhausting to force creativity even when you have nothing to express. You do not need to write a memoir or find a new \"calling\" to verify if your old path was right, because the only true way to test if your creative identity is gone is to sit with this exhaustion without trying to solve it immediately, rather than immediately trying to \"fix\" it with more words or efforts.",
